{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L48"},"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"title":"HTTPDestination","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"}],"externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as one request."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/Destination-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","text":"HTTPTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next sent only once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the previous one has a response or has failed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The method is ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record, then ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/context"},{"type":"text","text":", so a server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names are the instrument’s: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traceparent"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracestate"},{"type":"text","text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument"},{"type":"text","text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, where a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" writes it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", whatever a configured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field or the instrument wrote.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body"},{"type":"text","text":" for the batch’s records, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived. Any other status, or no response,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"means it didn’t; either way the batch is not sent again.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record can still arrive twice: one a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") may have arrived before. Its "},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" handles its own failures: a batch the encoder can’t encode, a send that gets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no response and a response that isn’t 2xx are each logged at error level and dropped, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the delivery and its other destinations carry on. A cancelled delivery cancels the send in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flight, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns without logging it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/Destination-Implementations":{"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","title":"Destination Implementations","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/Destination-Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/destination-implementations"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/receive(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Sends ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the endpoint as one request, and logs a failure.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"receive(_:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/receive(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"receive"},{"kind":"text","text":"(["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/Destination":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"}],"navig